---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';

// Drafted to describe what this site actually does — the contact form posts to
// Web3Forms, fonts come from Google, and the host sits behind Cloudflare.
// Still worth a lawyer's eye before you rely on it.
const updated = '22 August 2026';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated={updated}>
  <p>
    This policy explains what {site.name} collects when you use
    <strong>ekstechub.com</strong>, why we collect it, and what you can ask us to do
    with it. It covers the website only — information you give us during a paid
    engagement is governed by that engagement's own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect two kinds of information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What you send us.</strong> When you submit the contact form we receive
      the division you selected, your name, your email address, your phone or WhatsApp
      number if you provide one, and the content of your message. If you contact us by
      email, phone or WhatsApp instead, we receive whatever that channel passes on.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> Our host and its content delivery network
      record standard server logs — IP address, browser type, pages requested and
      timestamps — for security and reliability. We do not run advertising trackers, we
      do not use cookies to profile you, and we do not build behavioural profiles of
      visitors.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiry and route it to the right division.</li>
    <li>To carry out work you have asked us to quote for or deliver.</li>
    <li>To keep records of enquiries and engagements for business and tax purposes.</li>
    <li>To protect the site against abuse and spam.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information, and we do not send marketing to people who only
    ever made an enquiry.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    We share your information only with the service providers that make the site work,
    and only to the extent they need it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> — processes the contact form and delivers submissions to our inbox.</li>
    <li><strong>Our hosting provider and Cloudflare</strong> — serve the site and keep server logs.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — serves the typefaces this site uses; your browser requests them directly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information where the law requires it. Otherwise we do not pass
    your details to anyone, including other clients.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not become engagements are kept for up to two years, so we can pick
    up a conversation you return to. Records relating to actual engagements are kept for
    as long as the law requires us to retain business and tax records. Server logs are
    kept for a short period by our providers under their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to show you what we hold about you, correct anything that is wrong, or
    delete it where we are not legally required to keep it. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="underline">{site.contact.email}</a>
    and we will respond within 30 days. If you ask us to delete an enquiry we will do so
    unless it relates to a live or recently completed engagement.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS and form submissions are encrypted in transit. No system
    is perfectly secure, so please do not send sensitive financial details, identity
    documents or passwords through the contact form — we will tell you a safer route if an
    engagement needs them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of this page. Material
    changes will be noted here rather than made quietly.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions go to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="underline">{site.contact.email}</a>,
    or write to us at {site.contact.address}, {site.contact.region}.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm border-t border-outline-variant pt-6 mt-10">
    <strong>Note for the site owner:</strong> this draft describes how the site currently
    behaves. Have a lawyer confirm it against Cameroonian data-protection requirements —
    and against any additional processors you add later — before treating it as final.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
